---
import Layout from '../layouts/MinimalLayout.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import { SITE_DATA } from '../constants';

import ContactForm from '../components/ContactForm.astro';

import '../styles/home.css';
import '../styles/about.css';
---

<Layout pageTitle="NYC Physics Tutor">
	<Hero 
		name={SITE_DATA.name} 
		tagline="Physics Tutoring with 20+ Years of Experience" 
		twitter={SITE_DATA.twitter}
		linkedin={SITE_DATA.linkedin}
		scholar={SITE_DATA.scholar}
		email={SITE_DATA.email}
	/>

    <div class="page-container">
        <div class="about-content">
            <div class="about-intro-wrapper centered-column">
                <p class="intro-text">
                    Since 2003, I've provided expert one-on-one instruction for high school and university students across New York City. You will benefit from my deep familiarity with local curricula, access to rigorous problem sets, and a patient approach that is entirely tailored to how you learn.
                <br><br>
                    Call or text me at <a href="tel:+17187537060">718-753-7060</a>, email me at <a href={`mailto:${SITE_DATA.email}`}>cjhellwig@gmail.com</a>, or use the <a href="#contact">contact form</a> below. Let’s map out a plan for your upcoming tests and coursework. Reach out today to discuss your goals and schedule a session. 
                </p>
            </div>

            <section>
                <h2>Proven Experience in NYC’s Top Schools</h2>
				<p class="intro-text">
					I’ve been tutoring physics and math in New York City for over two decades. Because I work extensively with students from top local independent and prep schools—including Trinity, Dalton, Chapin, and Horace Mann—as well as with undergraduates and post-bacs at NYU and Columbia, I know the exact pacing, rigor, and expectations of your physics syllabus.
					<br><br>
					Whether you are tackling a high school intro course, AP Physics C E&M, or your college-level physics pre-med requirements, I already know the hurdles you are facing because I’ve helped dozens of students clear them.
				</p>
			</section>

            <section>
                <h2>The Approach: Experience, Patience, and Vast Resources</h2>
				<p class="intro-text">
					I’ve explained these concepts thousands of times, to thousands of students, in every way imaginable. If an explanation doesn't click the first time, we simply try another angle—patience is a core part of how I work. You won't just get a patient guide; you’ll get access to a massive library of curated practice problems, past exams, and targeted problem sets. Instead of last-minute cramming, we use targeted practice problems and real exam material so you can walk into test day fully prepared.
				</p>
			</section>

            <section>
                <h2>Subjects Covered</h2>
                <ul class="education-list icon-list">
                    <li>
                        <span class="list-item-title">High School</span>
                        <span class="list-item-description">AP Physics 1, 2, and C (Mechanics & E&M)—with a strong track record of helping students secure a 5 on the exam—alongside Honors Physics and other advanced school tracks, including support for students at Trinity, Dalton, Horace Mann, Chapin, and other NYC schools.</span>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <span class="list-item-title">College & University</span>
                        <span class="list-item-description">First-year General Physics I & II (Algebra and Calculus-based)—frequently supporting pre-med students and undergraduates from NYU and Columbia through their foundational science requirements.</span>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </section>

            <section>
				<h2>Testimonials</h2>
				<p>"Two months before the AP Physics 1 exam, my son Nate thought he was fine self-studying with a chatbot. Then he took a practice test, bombed it, and completely panicked. A family friend told me to call C.J.. They spent eight straight weeks on Zoom together, doing intense sessions late into the night. Nate went from completely lost to getting a 5 on the exam. If your kid is in over their head, just hire C.J."
					<br>– David Z.
				</p>
				<p class="intro-text">"C.J. helped me understand concepts in just minutes from Professor Shaevitz' Physics I Course at Columbia University that I would otherwise never have understood. Even though he started tutoring me in the middle of the semester, meeting with C.J. improved my grade significantly, and I actually retained the material as opposed to forgetting it once the course ended. For anyone struggling with physics or any other subjects, definitely contact C.J.!"
					<br>– Marielle Johnson
				</p>
			</section>

            <section id="contact">
                <h2>Ready to Master Physics and Raise Your Grades?</h2>
				<p class="intro-text">
                    Call or text me at <a href="tel:+17187537060">718-753-7060</a>, email me at <a href={`mailto:${SITE_DATA.email}`}>cjhellwig@gmail.com</a>, or use the contact form below. Let’s map out a plan for your upcoming tests and coursework. Reach out today to discuss your goals and schedule a session. 
				</p>
				<div class="contact-form-section">
		            <ContactForm source="Physics Landing Page"/>
        		</div>
			</section>


        </div>
	</div>
</Layout>
